From: CoolFreeze23 <34906576+CoolFreeze23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: queue every device on a rootPD restart

The AFTER_POWERUP notifier of a crashed rootPD queues group recovery
through ath12k_ahb_queue_group_recovery(), but skipped a device whose
reset work was busy. With the reset request of patch 350, a pending
reset work can be a stale run that returns at once, so the request of
the rootPD crash was lost and the group stayed down. Requesting the
reset before the busy test is not enough: a running work that already
consumed its request does not run again, and a plain set_bit() followed
by the work_busy() read lacks the ordering that queue_work()'s PENDING
test-and-set gives every other queueing path.

Request the reset and queue the work for every device: a run whose
request was answered by a later group power-up, or that finds no
request, returns at once. Correct the comment.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
@@ -967,7 +967,11 @@ static void ath12k_ahb_release_crashed_u
  * was waiting for it holds ag->mutex and consumes rootpd_crashed, so the
  * marker is re-checked under the mutex: if it is still set, no power-up
  * picked the restart up (none ran yet, or it timed out) and recovery is
- * still owed. Devices whose reset work is queued or running are skipped.
+ * still owed.
+ * In both cases every device's reset is requested and its work queued,
+ * also when it is queued or running already: a run whose request was
+ * answered by a later group power-up, or that finds no request, returns
+ * at once (ath12k_core_reset()), so an extra run costs nothing.
  */
 static void ath12k_ahb_queue_group_recovery(struct ath12k_base *ab,
 					    bool new_crash)
@@ -993,9 +997,11 @@ static void ath12k_ahb_queue_group_recov
 		set_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &partner_ab->dev_flags);
 		set_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_RECOVERY, &partner_ab->dev_flags);
 
-		if (!new_crash && work_busy(&partner_ab->reset_work))
-			continue;
-
+		/*
+		 * queue_work() also when the work is busy: its ordered PENDING
+		 * test-and-set makes the run that follows see the request, and
+		 * a queued work may be a stale run that would return without it.
+		 */
 		set_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_RESET_REQUESTED, &partner_ab->dev_flags);
 		queue_work(partner_ab->workqueue_aux, &partner_ab->reset_work);
 	}
